1. Project Overview & Tech Stack

This project is the official web application for Brit Institute, a UK-based training institute specializing in Data Analytics, Data Science, and AI.

Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router)
 with React 19 & TypeScript.
Styling: Tailwind CSS v4
 with custom brand design tokens (gold #D4AF37, deep dark brand purple #24101F, orange #D95700, etc.).
Animation & Visuals: Framer Motion
 (for animated chatbot transitions and modal animations) and Three.js / React Three Fiber
 (for 3D graphics).
Communication & Cloud Services: AWS SES (@aws-sdk/client-sesv2) for transactional emails and leads notification.
Tracking & Analytics: Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics 4, and Meta Pixel with client-side event deduplication.
2. High-Level Architecture & Request Flow
3. Detailed Breakdown of Key Modules


A. Root Layout & Multi-Variant Routing (app/layout.tsx)
Host & Subdomain Awareness: Using getRequestSiteConfig, the app can serve both the main site (britinstitute.uk) and a dedicated standalone chatbot (chat.britinstitute.uk or /career-chatbot).
SEO & JSON-LD Schemas: Every page receives structured schemas (lib/seo.ts) such as EducationalOrganization, WebSite, Course, and FAQPage to enhance Google SERP visibility.
Persistent Layout Overlays: Injects global floating elements on every page:
TopBanner (announcement countdown bar with dismiss storage).
Navbar (responsive navigation with course catalog fetch).
GlobalUI (global click handler for conversion CTAs).
CareerChatbotFloat (AI career advisor widget).
WhatsAppFloat (direct link to UK admissions WhatsApp).
StickyBottomBar (quick call/inquiry bar).


B. Home Page Experience (app/page.tsx & app/HomePageClient.tsx)
Query Parameter Triggers: If a visitor arrives via an ad link containing ?apply=true or ?form=1, OpenOfferModalOnMount fires a custom window event brit:open-offer-modal immediately to prompt the user.
Main Section Composition: Rendered inside BritInspiredHome.tsx:
Hero Section: Value proposition, UK job focus, trust metrics.
Career Journey Strip: Visual 5-step roadmap from learning to placement.
Logo Strip & Trust Badges: Employer logos and hiring partners.
Product Cards & Courses: Sliced from coursesData (Data Analytics, Data Science, Agentic AI, Generative AI).
Feature Suite: Skills, hands-on portfolio proof, career transition support.
Reviews, Portfolios & FAQ Accordion: Interactive FAQ (FAQ.tsx) with schema markup.


C. Global CTA Interceptor & Modal System (components/layout/GlobalUI.tsx)

Rather than wiring an onClick handler on every individual button across the site:

GlobalUI listens to all document clicks.
If a clicked element is a CTA button/link containing phrases like "Apply Now", "Enroll", "Register", "Talk to Career Expert", or class .btn-gold, it intercepts the click and opens OfferModal.
This provides consistent lead capture without code duplication.


D. Dynamic Course Routing (app/courses/[slug]/page.tsx)
SSG Pre-rendering: generateStaticParams pre-renders routes for data-analytics, data-science, ai-automation, and gen-ai.
Hybrid Data Layer: Reads rich static course information from courseData.ts and falls back/enhances with live data via fetchCourseBySlug.
Course Modules Included:
Tool tech-stack badges (Excel, SQL, Power BI, Python, Pandas, etc.).
Dedicated interactive curriculum views (DataAnalyticsCurriculum.tsx, AgenticAICurriculum.tsx, etc.).
Brochure instant download tracking (BrochureDownloadButton.tsx).
Embedded lead capture form (CourseLeadForm.tsx).


E. AI Career Chatbot (CareerChatbotFloat.tsx & lib/careerChatbot.ts)
Acts as a digital career counsellor for prospective students.
Step-by-Step Question Flow: Tracks stages (S0 to S7) assessing experience level, current background, tool familiarity (SQL, Excel, Python), timeline, and target role.
Calculation Engine: computeAssessmentResult analyzes the student's inputs, identifies skill gaps, calculates projected UK salaries, and recommends the best-fitting program.
Lead Generation: Collects student contact information and pushes leads to the admissions CRM.


F. Lead Capture & AWS SES Email Pipeline (app/api/course-registration/route.ts)

When a user submits a registration or brochure form:

Validation: Checks required fields (name, email, phone, course, purpose).
CRM Forwarding: Posts the lead directly to the main API endpoint (api.britinstitute.uk/api/leads).
AWS SES Notification: Calls sendCourseRegistrationEmail to send an HTML-formatted notification email via Amazon SES to the admissions team.
Analytics: Client triggers trackLead pushing an event with a unique ID to Google Tag Manager and Meta Pixel (fbq).
